# dbgenv OnceLock — cache presence-only debug env vars off the hot paths

date:   2026-09-17
host:   lilith (WSL, x86_64-linux)
base:   17cbbf7f (main tip; parent of this commit)
cand:   this commit. crates/svtav1-encoder/src/dbgenv.rs grew 17
        presence-flag accessors; every remaining raw `std::env::var_os`/
        `var(...).is_ok()` presence check on per-block-or-hotter paths now
        reads the OnceLock cache. svtav1-dsp gained two local OnceLock
        gates (ZZ_CHROMA_ROW / ZZ_CHROMA_DBG in port_pd_pred.rs).
tool:   tools/perf_ab.sh — interleaved paired rounds, randomised order,
        neither side niced. perf record -F 4999 for the symbol shares.
data:   benchmarks/dbgenv_once_2026-09-17.raw.tsv

WHY. A 24K-sample `perf record` of `perf_encode gradient 512 512 40 6`
(/tmp/perf_had.data) put `__getenv` + `std::env::var_os` at ~3.5 % of
encode cycles — `quant::optimize_b` re-read `SVTAV1_TRELLIS` on EVERY
trellis coefficient. The same pattern sat in ~25 more debug gates on
per-(block, candidate, txb, ref) paths (SKIPDBG x6, MRGDBG x2, MEDBG x2,
RDOQDBG, COEFFDBG, LAMDUMP, WINDBG, INTERDBG, NSQSRCH, PD0PRED, QLEV_CO,
FHDBG, LFDBG, RPSDBG x2, SVT_MFMV_DBG x2, ZZ_TPL). dbgenv.rs existed to
finish exactly this job; these were the leftovers. Value-carrying vars
(SVTAV1_RECON_BIN, _VB_DUMP, _RECON10_BIN, _LRREC_BIN, _FHDUMP,
_FCTX_OUT, _SC_TOOLS, _DBG_MI, SVT_HDR_MODE, predict.rs's pin vars)
stay where they are — the module documents that contract.

Semantics: presence flags are read once per process; setting one
mid-encode no longer takes effect. Every caller is a shell-driven stderr
dump that exports before launch — nothing loses a capability. Verified
SVTAV1_TRELLIS=1 still prints 1626 TREL lines on gradient 128 and
SVTAV1_SKIPDBG+SVTAV1_RDOQDBG print on gradient 64.

RESULT — every cell ident=Y (byte-identical bitstream), every p25/p75
span disjoint from 1.0:

  cell          n    base_ms    cand_ms   ratio    speedup
  512 p6        15     26.697     25.389   0.9549   1.047x
  256 p2        11    184.561    160.924   0.8734   1.145x
  256 p10       11      1.569      1.458   0.9360   1.068x
  512 p2        11    376.925    342.911   0.9065   1.103x
  512 p10       11      7.159      6.798   0.9520   1.050x

Larger wins at p2 because more candidates per block means more
SKIPDBG/RDOQDBG/TRELLIS gate reads per encode.

Post-change profile (/tmp/perf_cand.data, 12,464 samples): getenv +
env wrappers 0.06 % total (was ~3.5 %).

Also folds in a `cargo fmt` normalisation: HEAD was fmt-dirty under the
CI-pinned 1.98 rustfmt (files untouched by this change — encdec_arm.rs,
inject.rs, tx_gates.rs — reflowed), so the tree now passes
`cargo fmt --all --check`.

gates: regression_spotcheck.sh 141/141; nextest on the two touched
       crates 3412/3412; cargo fmt --all --check clean;
       tools/clippy_inventory.sh --check rc=0.
